    "body": "In `secp256k1_silentpayments_sender_create_outputs`, output keys are currently generated by calling `secp256k1_eckey_pubkey_tweak_add`. That helper delegates to `secp256k1_ecmult`, which does a full Straus W-NAF scalar multiplication with GLV decomposition and up to 129 point doublings per output, followed by an immediate modular inversion in `secp256k1_ge_set_gej`.\n\nBecause `ctx->ecmult_gen_ctx` is already validated on entry, we can compute `t_k * G` with `secp256k1_ecmult_gen_gej` from the generator table and add `B_spend` with a single mixed addition (`secp256k1_gej_add_ge`). This drops all point doublings from the tweak calculation.\n\nTo avoid the individual field inversions, we collect the Jacobian points in batches of up to 16 outputs and convert them simultaneously via Montgomery batch inversion (`secp256k1_ge_set_all_gej_var`), like we already do for label candidates in the scanning path. This cuts modular inversions down to one per 16 outputs.\n\nPasses all BIP-352 test vectors and existing tests. In local benchmarks, this reduces runtime by roughly 12% to 23% depending on output batch size.\n",
