      "message": "silentpayments: optimize sender output creation with generator table and batch inversion\n\nIn secp256k1_silentpayments_sender_create_outputs, output keys are\ngenerated by calling secp256k1_eckey_pubkey_tweak_add. That helper\ndelegates to secp256k1_ecmult, executing full Straus W-NAF scalar\nmultiplication with up to 129 point doublings and a standalone modular\ninversion per output, even though ecmult_gen_ctx is already validated\non entry.\n\nSwitch to secp256k1_ecmult_gen_gej to evaluate t_k * G from the generator\ntable and add B_spend with a single mixed addition (secp256k1_gej_add_ge).\nTo avoid individual field inversions, collect the Jacobian points in batches\nof up to 16 outputs and convert them simultaneously via Montgomery batch\ninversion (secp256k1_ge_set_all_gej_var), mirroring the batching used for\nlabel candidates in the scanning path.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Yudistira Putra",
        "email": "85178972+Yudis-bit@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-20T08:25:50Z"
