      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Concept ACK, tested 85ee5f5: it gives the same outputs as master, and `sender_create_outputs` takes 7% less time for one output, 14-15% less for 10-100 outputs with distinct scan keys and 29-35% less when they share one. I compared master, this PR and an independent Python implementation on the BIP352 sending vectors and 500 random sends, and timed both builds; script available. Question: the `secp256k1_ecmult_gen_gej` result now goes through `secp256k1_ge_set_all_gej_var`; is that intended? Its coordinates carry the context's blinding, the library converts them in constant time elsewhere, and `secp256k1_ge_set_all_gej` would fit here.\n",
